t(3, 1385, """When our father Adam and our mother Eve (peace be upon them) came down to earth to begin their great mission, which has not ended to this day, their first task was building the family home, not building a state, nor an army, nor creating a political-military entity on earth to be used as tools for the vicegerency of Adam, who was charged with leading the mission. He (peace be upon him) was the first vicegerent on earth and came down to establish this vicegerency, yet the home and the building of the human personality were the first stage of the duty of vicegerency on earth! So why did he not have children in his Paradise and then come down with his wife and children, so that they would directly found the tribe, which counts as a political, military and economic component par excellence, and vicegerency would begin in its complete form from the very first day?!

One of the reasons that can be drawn out by reflection tells us that the first field a human enters on his way to vicegerency on earth is not the field of his university education, nor his specialization, nor his wealth and money, nor his lineage, nor any component before the component of behavioral building that began in the home of Adam and Eve (peace be upon them), then progressed with the emergence of the small nucleus, "the children".

Your vicegerency on earth, then, is not attained without building you, and every human built wrongly will have no role in vicegerency on earth. For as the first era began, so the last era will be: a pure, clean home, for a husband who leads the morals of the family and of life; he advises, guides, excuses, helps, forgives and directs, then moves on to the wider stage: the family, the tribe, then society.

The foundation of the structure and the building, then, lies in making the vicegerent who will be one of perhaps hundreds of thousands of vicegerents on earth, all of whom attained true upbringing, just like Adam (peace be upon him), and attained morals, truthfulness and the establishing of justice. And because vicegerency on earth is of great standing while people reckon it easy, it is given to thousands, not to millions of people, for disciplining behavior and morals is not within everyone's reach.

In his home Adam (peace be upon him) practiced his morals; his pure-natured wife learned from him, then his children and grandchildren learned from him; among them were the righteous and among them were those less than that.

And thus the first field of vicegerency on earth begins with your personal life: with yourself, your tongue and your chastity; your conduct and your purity; your morals with the one who does good and with the one who does wrong; the purity of your heart when you sleep; and …""")

t(4, 60, """… your hatred of injustice and your repelling it without general strife, your steadfastness upon justice, and your establishing justice upon yourself before people.

Without this, millions of humans pass on to the Hereafter never having been made vicegerents on earth at all, because they thought the matter was a tongue, an arm and rabble-rousing!""")

h(4, 650, """The home and the building of the human: vicegerency on earth is not a tongue and an arm!""")

t(4, 1390, """The most famous imams of hadith science split into two camps over the hadith "A father is not killed for his child"; the great majority of the earlier master hadith scholars ruled it (((weak))) and not established from the Prophet ﷺ.

The views of the most famous earlier and contemporary hadith scholars on weakening this hadith, which is dangerous in forming a deviant idea about alleged, imaginary rights of fathers and mothers:
1. The earlier imams (who weakened the hadith)
The great hadith critics held that the chains of this hadith are feeble and not free of a defect that undermines its authenticity:

* Imam Ali ibn al-Madini (al-Bukhari's teacher): He found the hadith defective and stated plainly that it is not authentic.
* Imam al-Tirmidhi: He said in his Sunan: "This is a hadith with inconsistency in it," and mentioned that its chain contains narrators whose memory was criticized (such as Isma'il ibn Muslim).
* Imam Ibn Abd al-Barr: He affirmed that the hadith is inconsistent in its chain.
* Imam Abd al-Haqq al-Ishbili and Ibn al-Qattan: Among the scholars of the Maghreb who explicitly stated the weakness of this hadith's chains.
* Shaykh al-Islam Ibn Taymiyyah: He indicated that the hadiths on not killing a father for his child are defective and not established in narration, and are not strong enough to oppose the Qur'anic text.
------------------------------
2. Among contemporary scholars:

* Shaykh Ahmad Shakir: He agreed with the earlier scholars and affirmed that the hadith is weak and cannot be used as evidence.
* Shaykh Muhammad ibn Salih al-Uthaymin: He stated that the hadith is very weak, and described the rational-juristic reason some relied on (that the father is the cause of the son's existence) as "a dead reason", affirming the obligation of executing the father by the general rulings of the Qur'an.
------------------------------
Summary of the hadith scholars' view
The settled view among the verifying hadith scholars is that the hadith is defective and weak in its chain.
For this reason contemporary Arab courts and laws set its penalty based on the strict Qur'anic verses, treating the father as a deliberate killer who deserves the death penalty, and the mother likewise.""")

h(5, 400, """No license for a father or mother to deliberately kill their children""")

t(5, 1160, """In recent years, and especially in the last 15 years, individuals have become active in the Ummah whose daily concern is how to bring down the four Rightly Guided Caliphs in the eyes of the Ummah's youth by presenting them as having committed errors. Consequently, the result they want to bring the Ummah to is that the Ummah believes the Prophet ﷺ disowned them, may Allah be pleased with them.

Those who malign the four Rightly Guided Caliphs are two camps:

The first is the camp that tried to convey the idea that the Prophet ﷺ was not pleased with al-Siddiq, al-Faruq and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them, exploiting the fact that most people do not focus on distinguishing between the ijtihad of a human who is right and wrong, and the goodness of his inner self. This camp strove to distort the goodness of the two Shaykhs and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them, and of the Companions of our Prophet ﷺ, as this camp tried to make a large number in the Ummah imagine that the three caliphs turned back on their heels after the death of the Prophet ﷺ.

The second camp is led by the chief of modern-day Nasibis, Sabir Mashhur, who for years tried to convey to his Nasibi followers that the Prophet ﷺ was not pleased with Imam Ali, peace be upon him!

They all lied .. For the first vision I ever saw in my life, which, praise be to Allah, I know is a true vision, Allah willing, expressed the opposite of this cheap accusation against the four Rightly Guided Caliphs.

The mosque of the Prophet ﷺ was of mud bricks and clay as in old times, and what lay before it and around it was ground like the ground of past ages .. The mosque was as it truly was .. It was that distant time ... The vision took me 1450 years back .. We were standing in a near semicircle, only the Prophet ﷺ and the four Rightly Guided Caliphs, and they were smiling and laughing lightly, and the Prophet ﷺ was never angry with them .. I was standing among them, seeing them, may Allah be pleased with them, standing at ease and with self-confidence, and they were joking with me as a grown adult jokes with a small child. Had they broken faith, as the people of falsehood accuse them, they would have stood before the Prophet ﷺ with bowed heads, but in the vision they stood with full self-confidence, the confidence of the Companion, may Allah be pleased with them. Some will say it is a vision, and I say it is one that confirmed to me, from the far realm of the unseen, the lie of those who make false claims against the four Rightly Guided Caliphs, especially as the main targets are al-Siddiq, al-Faruq and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them. Whoever does not understand the meaning of a vision, nothing will benefit him, for we know the extent of the denial of the unseen in minds. But it is a scene about 25 years old, yet as if seen a minute ago .. not a single detail of it has faded .. They, may Allah be pleased with them, were standing while taking direction from the Prophet ﷺ, and it was the direction of a leader who trusts those he directs .. They stood as true Companions .. as leaders, not as shaken or weak people.""")

t(6, 65, """Perhaps this vision will help those leaning toward believing the lies about the two Shaykhs and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them, in particular, for they are the most targeted for tarnishing their reputation. Do not believe them, for I know the scale of the attack and its ferocity. And whoever does not believe in the value of what a vision reveals, let him refrain from commenting, for any offense against the Rightly Guided Caliphs is unacceptable.""")

h(6, 700, """Do not believe them. This is how I saw the four Rightly Guided Caliphs""")

