t(7, 1440, """Modern means of communication have come to fulfill the aim of this prophetic etiquette for the traveler

The Prophet ﷺ and his Companions followed an orderly method full of mercy when entering Madinah after travel or campaigns.
1. Halting outside Madinah (waiting)
If the army or travelers reached the outskirts of Madinah at night, they did not enter it suddenly. Rather, they stopped at a place on the outskirts of Madinah called "al-Mu'arras", spent the night there and slept until morning.
2. Sending the bearer of good news (the herald)
The Prophet ﷺ would send a man ahead of the army into Madinah. This man would call out to the people and announce that the army was arriving in the morning. The aim of this was:

* That families rejoice at the safety of those returning.
* That women prepare and adorn themselves to receive their husbands.

3. Entering at forenoon
The Prophet ﷺ preferred to enter Madinah at forenoon (a short while after sunrise). He entered in broad daylight so that people could see one another clearly.
4. The welcome of children and women
When the army drew near Madinah, its people went out to welcome them joyfully. The children went out to meet the Prophet ﷺ and the travelers, and the Prophet ﷺ greeted them warmly and carried some of them with him on his mount out of tenderness and love for them.
5. Beginning with the mosque before the home
The first step the Prophet ﷺ took upon entering Madinah was going straight to the mosque. He entered the mosque and prayed two rak'ahs in it in gratitude to Allah for a safe return, then sat with the people a little, and after that went to his home.""")

h(8, 300, """How the Prophet ﷺ raised the Ummah!""")

t(8, 1030, """The general likeness may reach 95%, but in reality he is more beautiful and more radiant

His beard, peace be upon him, was lighter than this, and his mustache likewise lighter, when he descended .. The very same cut of this face! The general likeness and the structure of the face.

(For the first time in my life, today, I see this picture drawn in 1940, while reading about the history of drawing pictures of the Messiah.)

This picture was drawn by a Western artist who said he drew it after a dream he saw!

The features in my 2022 vision of the lord Messiah are very close to this picture. I will not say the facial features match, but the resemblance is very strong, perhaps reaching between 90 and 95%.

In my vision he was full of life more strongly than in this picture. His face was more radiant than this picture, with clear skin, and his handsomeness surpassed this picture by 20% more. His hair was soft. His facial features in the vision resemble this picture between 90 and 95%, but not 100% as in this picture. His nose was a little more beautiful than in this picture, and long as in this picture. His eyes did not have this sharpness; rather they were filled with longing and love, as if he had been yearning. His eyes were filled with a gaze that was all calm and serenity, with overwhelming, strong feelings of love whose intensity cannot be described, revealing an eagerness that dominated the body's movement. The skin was white tinged with red, not yellowish like this picture.

Summary:
The real image of the lord Messiah, peace be upon him, does not match the 1940 picture 100%, but it is astonishingly very close, and it greatly surprised me. The degree of closeness may reach 95%, taking into account the differences I wrote. But one who wishes to know the appearance of the lord Messiah can truly grasp a large part of his appearance through this picture. In the end, knowledge belongs to our Great Lord, first and last. But it is a true vision, Allah willing; I saw it in 2022. In it the Messiah came in color, bodily height and softness of hair as the Prophet ﷺ described him. This picture is extremely close to his noble face that I saw in that vision. Yet what is in this picture is not 100% the Messiah of my vision; the degree of resemblance reaches only 95%. The differences between my vision and this picture are not big differences, but they are "differences that carry weight", not trivial, making the real Messiah in my vision not match this picture.

Now, for the first time, the appearance of the lord Messiah, peace be upon him, can be imagined by one who has not seen him in a vision.""")

t(9, 1005, """Among the first pictures drawn of the lord Messiah, from the third century AD, that is, 250 years after his being raised to heaven, as the mural dates back!

The Church said: We draw the Messiah not with features we saw or knew, but with our understanding of the spirit of the Messiah!

The picture bears no relation to the lord Messiah, peace be upon him""")

